en:
For one variable define $\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\alpha=0,
\qquad
\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\theta=1,$ so that $\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}
(\alpha+\beta\theta)=\beta.$ For two variables, choose left derivatives and keep the canonical order $\theta_1\theta_2$: $\begin{aligned}\frac{\partial^L f}{\partial\theta_1}
&=\beta_1+\gamma\theta_2,\\
\frac{\partial^L f}{\partial\theta_2}
&=\beta_2-\gamma\theta_1.\end{aligned}$ The minus sign in the second line arises because the odd derivative must pass through $\theta_1$ before differentiating $\theta_2$.

ja:
一変数のとき、 $\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\alpha=0,
\qquad
\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\theta=1,$ と定義すると、 $\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}
(\alpha+\beta\theta)=\beta.$ 二変数のとき、左微分を選び、標準的順序 $\theta_1\theta_2$ を保つ： $\begin{aligned}\frac{\partial^L f}{\partial\theta_1}
&=\beta_1+\gamma\theta_2,\\
\frac{\partial^L f}{\partial\theta_2}
&=\beta_2-\gamma\theta_1.\end{aligned}$ 二行目のマイナス符号は、奇の微分が $\theta_2$ を微分する前に $\theta_1$ を通り抜けなければならないことから生じる。

zh:
对于一个变量，定义 $\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\alpha=0,
\qquad
\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\theta=1,$ 从而 $\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}
(\alpha+\beta\theta)=\beta.$ 对于两个变量，选择左导数并保持规范顺序$\theta_1\theta_2$： $\begin{aligned}\frac{\partial^L f}{\partial\theta_1}
&=\beta_1+\gamma\theta_2,\\
\frac{\partial^L f}{\partial\theta_2}
&=\beta_2-\gamma\theta_1.\end{aligned}$ 第二行中的负号出现，是因为奇导数必须先穿过$\theta_1$，然后才能对$\theta_2$求导。

